# iCloud Drive conflict copies ("foo 2.ts" beside "foo.ts"). These are generated
# silently whenever two agents write the same file, and an agent running
# `git add -A` will otherwise commit stale source. scripts/check-duplicate-files.js
# is the precise check (it only flags a copy sitting beside its own original);
# this is the blunt stop. Caveat: a file genuinely named "Part 2.md" needs
# `git add -f`.
* [0-9]
* [0-9].*

